// Selenium WebDriver — .NET bindings (Selenium.WebDriver.csproj).
//
// The .csproj uses Microsoft.NET.Sdk + custom signing
// (Selenium.snk) + assembly-info templating + multi-targeting
// (netstandard2.0). aeb's `dotnet.build_project` would regenerate
// the .csproj from setters and lose all of that, so the right
// builder is `dotnet.build_project_existing(b)` — runs
// `dotnet build` against the upstream .csproj unchanged.
//
// Selenium uses paket for NuGet pinning (`paket.dependencies`,
// `paket.lock`). aeb's lib/dotnet routes inline `nuget(...)` setters
// and registry .nupkg.ae artifacts; this conversion sidesteps that
// entirely by letting the upstream .csproj declare its own
// PackageReferences as it does today. paket-pinned closures end up
// resolved by `dotnet restore` (run implicitly as part of
// `dotnet build`).

import build
import dotnet

main() {
    b = build.start()
    dotnet.build_project_existing(b)
}
